# Server Components

Server Components are the default; introduce 'use client' only at the lowest and narrowest practical boundary that actually requires client-side behavior, and never move server-renderable code across that boundary merely to support an interactive descendant.

## Minimal Client Boundaries

- Place `'use client'` at the lowest practical component boundary that requires
  client-side functionality.
- Never convert a page, layout, section, or parent component to a Client Component
  solely because one descendant requires state, event handlers, effects, browser
  APIs, client hooks, or a client-only library.
- Extract interactive behavior into focused Client Components and keep
  non-interactive rendering, data fetching, secrets, and server logic in
  Server Components.
- Pass only necessary serializable data across the Server → Client boundary.
- Prefer Server Component composition through `children`/slots instead of moving
  server-renderable UI into the client module graph.
- Render Client Providers as deep in the component tree as practical.
- If `'use client'` can be removed from a component by extracting its interactive
  portion, it should be removed.